V1.1 RELEASE FEATURES
===========================================================================
GOALS:
    - data driven accuracy evaluation
    - usability
        - visual configurability
        - controls for memory usage
        - more disabled-by-default spells. most users will assume the addon doesn't work
          at all when certain spells don't work as they expect.
    - finish the few solvable complex cases (goak, vdh meta, avatar)


NOTES ON COMPLEX CASES -----------------------------------------------------------
    - [UPDATE] meta vs. apex is solved. now cheat death (should be easier)
    - AVATAR SHOULD BE HANDLED WITH UNCERTAIN=true
        - [UPDATE] just guessing that avatar on add is the real avatar is a decent approx. when proc>avatar
          happens, the potential differentiating signals are (a) total duration and (b) an update that happens
          "too fast". avatar updates for two reasons:
            * real avatar was pressed during proc avatar
            * tblast was pressed
          tblast has a 6s (reduced by haste) cooldown, which is where (b)'s "too fast" comes from. (a) can
          also be calculated but will be confused by things like bloodlust, which will allow many more
          avatar extensions than usual due to reduced tblast cooldown. [FOR NOW] treat avatar like every
          other extension ability, guessing that the ADD event is real avatar. as long as stand-alone proc
          avatars are not confused for real avatar, this approximation won't be noticeable since avatar has
          CDR anyway.
        - can't tell whether the proc or real buff was pressed until duration exceeds 4s.
          but it is unambiguous which buff is active, so just light it up immediately.
        - the AotS proc can't happen during avatar
        - is avatar of the storm properly tracked? needs testing
            - cast at 939.946
            - proc > avatar overwrites duration (sets to 20s), doesn't extend
            - avatar can update for 2 reasons: proc, +2s extension
            - if there is a proc, it must be the AURA(add) event
            - but if so, is it possible to determine which of the updates was the real avatar?
                - sad part is even if this can be figured out, avatar has CDR anyway so the timer won't be correct
            - avatar procs don't grant 2 thunder blast stacks
    - THE VDH META SPECIAL CASE: when meta extends, which ability was pressed first?
      this determines the cooldown. when apex>meta, the duration does not
      extend. when meta>apex, it does. so:
        t0=0: buff 1
        t1:   buff 2 (=meta buff is updated)
            if t1: >10s? then t0=meta, t1=apex  
            else:  <10s? if total duration = 30s, then t0=meta, t1=apex
                         if total duration < 30s, then t0=apex, t1=meta
        - Other weird observation: after putting meta on CD unambiguously and then
          procing the apex talent well after meta was over, meta was still considered off
          cooldown for some reason. This bug may have been an issue with not calling
          queueCooldown and is already fixed.
    certain=true
        [apex > meta]    doesn't happen
        meta > apex      don't do anything, don't infer on update. it is convinced meta
                         was cast and it is correct about the timing. it can ignore the
                         apex talent because it's just a meta extension
    certain=false
        apex > meta      duration < 30
        meta > apex      duration = 30

    - THE GIFT OF THE GOLDEN VALKYR SPECIAL CASE: gift of the golden valkyr can update
      goak. this should be easy because of the concurrent debuff
        - because this is recorded as an update to the previous goak
        - if goak is active -> cheat procs, goak never gets deglowed
            - goak gets overwritten by cheat on update because it's >1 charge
        - goak is usually IDed fast (certain=true) because only cheat matches flags and cheat requires debuff
            - should cheat return goak, certain=false?
        - cheat also often IDs since its only flag match is goak and cheat doesn't require a button press
        - overwrite/extend:
            - cheat > goak: overwrite (becomes 8s)
            - goak > cheat: weird extend (becomes 12s no matter goak's dur, seems like a bug)
            - goak > goak: overwrite (becomes 8s)
        - ok, so then these should almost always resolve correctly because of certainty. the only
          chance for messing up is a random debuff landing within tolerance or happening to press
          a button within tolerance of cheat
        - cheat does not glow goak. so it also never deglows goak. seems glowing goak is the better thing
          to do, similar to that dh talent
        MORE NOTES FROM A DIFFERENT DISCUSSION ----------------
        - in uncertain cases: C=cheat, G=GoAK
            CASE: C>G where G cast is close enough to C proc that can't determine which was which
                  need a VDH-like "return GoAK even though it could be cheat"
                  if uncertain, then the two abilities were used so close together that we can't
                  discern which caused the debuff. so just assign arbitrarily. first can always
                  be GoAK. the CD will be off by fractions of a second.
            ^^^ this won't work because we can't distinguish C>G from G>G without C's duration.
                a debuff is not POSITIVE evidence of C - but lack of a debuff is POSITIVE evidence of G by excluding C
                no spellcast is POSITIVE evidence of C - excludes G, leaving only C
                REQUIRES CONSUMPTION TO AUTOMATICALLY RESOLVE (ARBITRARILY)
    - avatar
        - avatar proc can't occur during avatar, meaning two things:
            a. no procs during avatar
            b. no procs during PROCS
        - every tblast is an aura update and a new event, will be LOTS of events in this batch
        - tblast has the same cooldown as tclap (6s, scales with haste)
            - this constrains number of extensions for both AotS and avatar.
            - AotS: 6s base, 10s max (2 exts): extension 1 -> 8s allowing for cd to finish and cast 2nd
                * need >50% haste to get a 3rd. prob happens during lust
        - since each update = new event, every update that isn't IDed will get sent to the history tray
          batch logic needs prune out extra events to prevent this
            - similar to VDH meta where the apex talent cd isn't tracked, AotS' cooldown also is untracked
            - so the batch logic just needs to determine if the event was long enough for a real avatar to
              put on cd. unfortunately it probably can't be determined whether avatar occurred on the
              AURA(add) or was a proc>avatar. so the exact start of the CD often won't be possible. can take
              the worst case approach and always assume first. an exact CD timer won't matter since there is
              dynamic CDR anyway.
    - goak
    - vdh meta
    - sentinel
        - this is already handled but in a hamfisted way. prevented from AURA(update) by charges=1
          and naturallyUpdates=true. which is another way of saying updates aren't of interest.
        - just need to prevent this from filling up the history tray. not a complex ability
