    - export serialized string: ~6MB
    - compressed string: 600kB

- required buff is only binary, so abilities with multiple required buffs
  (e.g., wake of ashes: HoW talent and shield talent each give a different buff)
  don't look for the extra buffs.
    - requires :consume()

- 260s cooldown on GoAK? what?
    - the first charge coincided
      with a random debuff from a mob and thus could not exclude cheat death.
      the second charge IDed almost instantly (application+tolerance) because a
      debuff did not randomly coincide with it.
        - this caused the second charge to be queued in trackCooldown first,
          which made the first charge's "availableAt" time AFTER the second charge.
        - the events are expired in order in manageEvents, so the first event's
          later availableAt is used in queueCooldown's :SetCooldown
    - a hack could be to allow queueCooldown to set the swipe if the proposed
      startTime is < the current start time
        - this hack doesn't fix the incorrect cooldown time though. in this goak
          example, the first charge is off by 4s (time to exclude cheat death)
    - this should be a very rare bug. very few people probably have the goak issue I
      have (bound to mousewheel so both charges fire off back to back).
    - the correct fix is to change cdfifo to record start times and have it
      re-solve cooldowns when new abilities are added
        - this relates to the cooldown backpropagate idea

