- cooldown backpropagation: comment from infer
    - let cooldowns back-propagate. e.g. bubble and wings cast close together: bubble 1st
      is not IDable. wings 2nd (during bubble) is IDable b/c of lack of debuff. once wings is
      IDed, it will be entered into the CD tracker, but starting after bubble. so we can infer
      that wings was not the button press at the time of bubble, but the current method of
      detecting off-cd abilities will still (correctly) say that wings was available when bubble
      was pressed.
        - the logic needs to be: IF the ability was pressed then, would that violate other known
          CD info?

