- [NOT SURE - this is a valid idea, but it is very rare to be unable to ID abilites
   after their duration completes]
    add logic layer to detect when all possible CDs have been cast
    - how useful is this? suppose at time X we know every ability is on
      cooldown. then when the next ability is used, can assume the best case
      scenario for every ability (min CD across all abilities).  this could
      eliminate some possibilities.  e.g., DK uses AMS at time=1 and IBF at
      time=10.  so at time=10 both are on CD.  the min CD across the two is
      40s, so until time=10+IBF's cooldown, anymore abilities from that player
      must have been AMS.
- confidence layer -> confidence network
    - the abstract idea for confidence should be that of a network. each confidence
      method should state its level of confidence and the decided ability, then the
      network should check itself for consistency.
- could we do better for the dreaded >1charge+CDR abilities?
    - the current behavior is to ignore CDR entirely. when used with full charges, the
      cooldown swipe begins and it propagates itself at the full CD timer. it is assumed
      that the next recharge doesn't start until the first recharge is completely full
        * can do better than this. each time the ability is observed is extra information
          that can help bring the timer closer to the truth.
        * currently the events are entirely ignored. the code just ensures that the
          numQueued counter never passes the max number of charges
- is it possible to track cold snap? can we infer that it was used when some other
  ability we can track comes off of cooldown unexpectedly? e.g., the ideal case would
  be when a mage casts spell 1 (unknown) immediately followed by spell 2 (inferred: ice
  cold) while ice cold was known to be on CD.
- get data to make better estimates on duration solve tolerance
    - both the "match" epsilon and the minimum difference
    - replays should enable this
    - probably changes from player to player depending on ping, FPS
- use updating to ID spells
    - e.g., fiery brand, sentinel constantly self-update
- better handle CDR
    - can compute upper bounds (or averages) on the amount of CDR gained. e.g., throwing
      avenger's shield on CD at 5 targets = 5s CDR per 12s (though procs reduce this
      and so does divine toll).:



ARCHITECTURE FEATURES ----------------------------------------------------------

INFERENCE ARCHITECTURE (maybe)
- instrumenting inferAbility suggested an Inference class that manages both the
  execution and record keeping for each inference could be beneficial.
    - replaces InferenceRecord
    - would store much of the data used and offer various ways of viewing/exporting it

ABILITY ARCHITECTURE (maybe)
- Abilities may need a formal object. Not yet convinced about this. This could be
  the solution to another arch issue about moving cooldown information out of the
  UI elements (swipe trackers)

- fold eventTrackers, cdTrackers and buffsForInference into Character.
    - buffsForInference: consider generalization to kicks, stops
    - empty eventTrackers and cdTrackers need to be easily creatable for ZKS

- [NOT SURE - is this really helpful?] better non-fixed duration support: generalize
  current FIXED, LTE, GTE system to a duration range (min, max) where the default
  FIXED idea is implemented as (duration-TOLERANCE, duration+TOLERANCE), LTE is min=0,
  GTE is max=Inf. some abilities surely have extensions that are short enough that this
  helps distinguish

- [LOW PRIORITY] multi-charge abilities and the history tray: this bug only
  exists someone disables the hide inaccurate trackers option between two
  casts of a multi-charge CDR ability. the bug shows a cooldown swipe for the
  sum of the two recharges, not the current recharge time.
  * the first ability goes to the history tray and does not call queueCooldown
    but *DOES* trigger the cooldown tracker. the second goes to the tracker via
    queueCooldown, which has numQueued=0. but because the first ability triggers
    the cdTracker, the endsAt time knows when the second charge will end and
    sets that as the cooldown duration.
  * interestingly, the startTime in this case is in the future, starting at
    the actual beginning of the last charge's recharge. the swipe stays at
    12 o'clock until the time passes future-cooldown, then begins and ends
    at the correct time for the second charge.

- groupSolutionUI
    - doesn't scale with non-5 member group tracking (raids/arenas)
    - isn't wide enough to handle things like groups with multiple paladins
    - doesn't show casters, so a multi-paladin group would have multiple freedoms
      but no indication that they are cast by different paladins


