- toward multiple inferences (e.g. for spells that update):
  the stuff below also fixed a corner case where non-certain initial inferences
  (right now, only metamorphosis) behaved incorrectly if the second inference
  did not find a confident match.
  add a "working guess"/uncertain state. isAbilityInferred() does not
  currently work correctly for !certainOnFirstInference abilities (meta),
  because it only tests whether the buff is named. this *happens* to work
  when the second inference is always successful, but in real world use there
  will be times when this fails. currently, uncertain inference only applies
  to meta and does:
    1. turns on meta's active glow when an uncertain inference is made
    2. at expiration, run inferAbility() again, but even if this fails it
       accepts the buff and runs finalize() because isAbilityInferred()
       doesn't check the uncertain status
    3. sets a cooldown swipe for the cross-ability maxCD on meta
    4. turns off the active glow on meta
  how this should work is:
    1. on apply: run infer()
        1a. infer=true|uncertain: trigger active glow
        1b. infer=true: finalize
        1c. infer=false: do nothing
    2. on expiry:
        2a. infer=true|uncertain: remove active glow
        2b: infer=true and wasn't finalized: finalize
        2c: infer=true: start cd swipe
        2d. infer=false: add to history tray
