* add logic layer for DH metamorphosis and new apex talent
    - special case where these two abilities both proc meta but can be
      distinguished by duration. so the logic layer would say: if there are
      only two possible remaining ability matches, if those two are only meta
      and apex talent, then light up the meta tracker no matter what. at the
      end of the buff, decide whether to start a cooldown timer.
    - adding this logic layer requires changing our mind about a buff inference
      at timeout. this could be done, but requires some rearchitecting. almost
      every part of the inference process is clean (meaning running another
      inferAbility wouldn't do anything wrong) except for:
        1. buff.caster
        2. cdTracker
      cdTracker is the worst problem for two reasons: (a) it is clobbered when
      the first inference happens meaning old CD info is lost and (b) it is
      supposed to be useful for OTHER inferences. the elegant way to handle
      this is to add an ability option to prevent tracking on first inference.
      should also move cdTracker maintenance out of InferenceEngine to keep
      reponsibilities cleanly delegated.
